    "payments": {
      "cardsAccepted": "limited",
      "cashImportance": "high",
      "text": "The UK Foreign Office describes Burundi as a largely cash-based society: take US dollars dated after 2006, as most businesses will not accept or exchange older notes and notes with small tears are rejected; euros and British pounds can usually be exchanged. Outside Bujumbura credit and debit cards are rarely accepted and there are not many ATMs, so do not rely on cash withdrawals; mobile money can often be used in tourist hotels. There is a shortage of foreign currency and an unofficial exchange rate that can differ substantially from the official one."
    },
    "safety": {
      "level": "high-risk",
      "text": "The UK Foreign Office advises against all travel to the Mugina, Cibitoke, Bukinyayana, Bubanza and Mpanda communes and to the RN6 and RN10 roads through the Kibira National Park, because of a rebel group and possible armed incursions from the DR Congo, and advises against travelling by road outside Bujumbura after dark. Canada advises avoiding non-essential travel to Burundi.",
      "source": {
        "url": "https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/burundi",
        "name": "UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office — Burundi travel advice",
